# =============================================================================
# rajkumar898.github.io — what does NOT go in a public repository
#
# The site is one file, index.html, plus the assets it references. Everything
# else in this folder is source material the tools in tools/ consume: photo
# and video originals, Word documents, the parked rebuild. None of it is
# served, all of it is large, and some of it should not be public at all.
#
# NOTHING IS DELETED by this file — every original stays on your disk exactly
# where it is. It simply is not committed.
#
# To check what git would actually keep, once the repo exists:
#     git status --porcelain --ignored=no
# =============================================================================

# ---- tooling -----------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- credentials: never, under any circumstances ------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
secrets.*
credentials.*

# ---- photo and video originals -----------------------------------------
# ~317 MB of full-resolution stills and phone videos. tools/build_media.py
# turns these into Photos/web/, which IS committed and is what the page loads.
Photos/*
!Photos/web/

# ---- project screen recordings -----------------------------------------
# ~754 MB of raw captures, four of them over 100 MB. The web copies live in
# assets/demos/ and assets/video/ and are committed.
projects/

# ---- the portrait original ---------------------------------------------
# 2 MB PNG; assets/profile.jpg is the copy the page uses.
profile photo/

# ---- the parked multi-page rebuild --------------------------------------
# A second, unfinished site. Publishing it alongside the real one would put
# two versions of your CV on the internet.
Updated_version/

# ---- documents ----------------------------------------------------------
# Your CV and project notes in editable form. The CV belongs on the site as
# a PDF you export deliberately, not as a .docx anyone can open and edit.
*.docx
*.doc
*.dotx
*.pptx
*.ppt
*.potx
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv

# ---- stray recordings at the repo root ----------------------------------
Recording *.mp4

# ---- the CV lives at assets/Raj-Kumar-CV.pdf, which is what the page links
# This root copy is the same file; committing both would leave two CVs on the
# site that can drift apart. The leading slash pins the rule to the root.
/Raj-Kumar-CV.pdf

# ---- papers: host the PDF only where the licence allows it --------------
# Every page of every PDF was searched for a licence statement. Only two carry
# one, and only those two are committed:
#
#   IEEE Access      creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0   -> committed
#   Energy Reports   creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0   -> committed
#   SETA             "(c) 2026 Published by Elsevier Ltd"  -> ignored, DOI only
#   IJACSA           no licence statement in 11 pages      -> ignored, DOI only
#   5 conference     no licence statement anywhere         -> ignored, page only
#
# The page links the ignored ones by DOI or publisher page, so nothing 404s.
# If a paper turns out to be open access after all, delete its line here and
# add `pdf:` back to its entry in index.html.
Published Paper PDFs/published conference papers/
Published Paper PDFs/published journal papers/3. Multi-tier*
Published Paper PDFs/published journal papers/4. Fungal Blast*

# The .png figures are the methodology-diagram masters; assets/pub-*.png are
# the resized copies the page shows. The certificates are already in
# assets/awards/.
Published Paper PDFs/**/*.png
Published Paper PDFs/**/*.jpeg

# ---- build leftovers ----------------------------------------------------
tools/_gallery.txt

# ---- image masters superseded by a web copy -----------------------------
jeju_contact_background.png

# ---- favicon masters; assets/favicon-*.png and favicon.ico are built from
# webpage_icon_3.png (the others are earlier drafts)
webpage_icon*.png

# ---- share-preview banner master; assets/og-image.jpg is built from it
main_image.png
